menu "USB UART bridge"

config BRIDGE_LUATOS
    bool "LuatOS ESP32-C3 CORE with a CH343 host interface"
    default n
    help
        Use UART0 for the onboard CH343 and UART1 for the target. The
        target TX starts isolated and accepts a single framed request.

config BRIDGE_INTERNAL_LOOPBACK
    bool "TEST ONLY: internal UART loopback with automatic initial arming"
    depends on !BRIDGE_LUATOS
    default n
    help
        Test image only. Route UART1 TX to RX inside the chip and automatically
        arm once after USB connects. GPIO1 remains an input with no pulls and
        no peripheral output routing, including while armed. No wire jumper is
        needed. BOOT still disarms, and a disconnect consumes the automatic arm.
        Never use this image for communication with an external UART.

endmenu
